# rMirror Agent Development Context

## What This Is

This is the **macOS agent** for rMirror. It is two parts:

- **rMirror for Mac 2.0** (`macos/`): a native Swift app (AppKit + SwiftUI, Swift package, no Xcode project) with the windows, menu bar item and updates.
- **The core** (`app/`): the Python application that monitors the reMarkable sync folder and uploads notebooks to the cloud backend. The Swift app runs it as a hidden child process in headless mode.

Status: 2.0 is on branch `claude/agent-native-app` in draft PRs and is not released (released agent: 1.7.0). The legacy 1.x menu-bar mode (rumps + Flask page in the browser) still builds but is **frozen** and will be removed in a follow-up. Sparkle has no key or feed yet; the Intel build has never been run.

Read first: `docs/native-app-architecture.md` (decisions), `docs/local-api.md` (contract between the two processes), `macos/README.md` (develop and package), `macos/docs/sparkle.md` (updates).

## Rules for the 2.0 app

- Never put the Python payload in `Contents/Frameworks` (signing fails); it lives in `Contents/Resources/core/`, each Mach-O signed first. Never sign with `--deep`.
- Build outside iCloud (a `com.apple.FinderInfo` xattr breaks `codesign --verify --strict`; `build_app.sh` refuses iCloud locations).
- The legacy UI is frozen: no features in `app/web/templates/index.html` or the rumps menu.
- Any new local route goes under `/api/v2` and is token-protected. Update `docs/local-api.md` before changing either side.
- Folder state: `missing` (folder does not exist) vs `unreadable` (exists, no Full Disk Access). Different screens.
- Password sign-in is gone. Sign-in starts from `POST /api/v2/auth/begin`.
- All user-facing wording lives in the Swift `*Copy` files; the core returns codes and numbers, never sentences.
- Readiness is only the `RMIRROR_CORE_READY` line on the core's stdout; the core exits when stdin closes.

## Tech Stack

- **Python 3.11+**: Core language
- **watchdog**: File system monitoring for reMarkable folder changes
- **Flask**: Web UI server (localhost:5555) for configuration
- **httpx**: Async HTTP client for API calls
- **rumps**: macOS menu bar app integration
- **Click**: CLI interface
- **Pydantic**: Configuration validation and settings management
- **keyring**: Secure credential storage in system keychain
- **PyInstaller**: Packaging into standalone .app bundle (`build_macos.sh` also creates, signs and notarizes the .dmg)

## Swift app (`macos/`)

```
macos/
├── Package.swift
├── Sources/
│   ├── RMirrorKit/         # library, no UI, unit-tested
│   │   ├── API/            # LocalAPIClient, models, enums, errors, MockLocalAPI (also holds the screen Fixtures)
│   │   ├── Core/           # CoreSupervisor (+ CoreLocator): start, watch, restart, stop the core
│   │   ├── Model/          # AppStore (state store), Stage (which screen to show), NotebookList
│   │   └── Copy/           # MainCopy, OnboardingCopy, SettingsCopy, SharedCopy: every user-facing string
│   └── RMirrorApp/         # executable
│       ├── App/            # RMirrorMain, AppDelegate, StatusItemController, WindowCoordinator, RootView,
│       │                   # LoginItem, Updater (Sparkle), ScreenRenderer (--render-screens)
│       ├── Onboarding/     # sign-in, missing reMarkable app, permission, first sync, progress, core problem
│       ├── Main/           # main window: header, notebook list, status, footer, notices
│       ├── Settings/       # settings window incl. developer options
│       └── Theme/
├── Tests/RMirrorKitTests/  # API, Copy (banned-words tests), Core, Model, Live (needs a running core)
├── Resources/Info.plist    # template
├── scripts/                # build_app.sh (build, assemble, sign, notarize, DMG), smoke_core.sh
├── docs/sparkle.md
└── build/                  # gitignored build output
```

How the pieces fit: `CoreSupervisor` launches the core (bundled in `Contents/Resources/core/`, or from the `RMIRROR_CORE_CMD` / `RMIRROR_CORE_ARGS` / `RMIRROR_CORE_CWD` override in development) with a fresh `RMIRROR_APP_TOKEN` and keeps stdin open. `LocalAPIClient` polls `GET /api/v2/state`; `AppStore` holds the result and `Stage.derive(core:state:guidedSyncActive:)` is the single place that decides which screen shows. Views never decide this themselves. `WindowCoordinator` and `StatusItemController` (menu bar item with "Open rMirror") sit on an AppKit lifecycle; the app has a Dock icon only while a window is open.

Commands: `swift build`, `swift test`, `.build/debug/RMirrorApp --render-screens <dir>`, `scripts/build_app.sh` (see `macos/README.md`; do not touch `macos/build/`).

**Add a screen:**
1. If it is a new state of the app, add a `Stage` case and its rule in `Stage.derive` (`RMirrorKit/Model/Stage.swift`), with a test.
2. Write the view in `RMirrorApp/Onboarding/` (or `Main/`, `Settings/`) and route to it from `RootView`.
3. Put every string in the right `*Copy` file (`OnboardingCopy`, `MainCopy`, `SettingsCopy`, `SharedCopy`) and run the Copy tests: they ban developer words (token, rate limit, callback, log, queue, quota, OCR, API, ...). Never put a string literal in a view.
4. Add a fixture state (`Fixtures` in `RMirrorKit/API/MockLocalAPI.swift`) and a line in `ScreenRenderer.screens()`; render with `--render-screens` and look at light and dark.

